    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>Embraced by Gustav Breidenstein in 1440, Wilhelm Waldburg was for centuries Blood Bound to his sire and ruled at his side. Convinced that Gustav's brutal, xenophobic rule endangered Berlin, Wilhelm engineered his sire's political fall and claimed West Berlin as Prince in his place &mdash; an act of betrayal that still causes him private grief despite his conviction that it was necessary. Under his rule, West Berlin has prospered and modernized, welcoming Kindred of every clan through an open-door policy that draws constant visitors and constant political risk. He punishes infractions with Blood Bonds and banishment rather than Final Death, a leniency Gustav considers weakness. His extra level of Presence lets him diffuse hostility in a room, forcing aggressors to spend Willpower and face higher difficulties while filling onlookers with unnatural calm.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Always smile. Treat everyone as a long-lost friend and take passionate interest in what they say. Never insult anyone, publicly or privately &mdash; the world has too many ears. Personal feelings don't matter; this is politics.</p>",
    "notes": "Haven: Charlottenburg Castle, West Berlin. Maintains at least friendly terms with every Kindred he encounters, including Nosferatu he visits personally in the sewers. Locked in an ongoing cold war with his sire and rival, Gustav Breidenstein, over who will rule a reunified Berlin.",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
